{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":64943,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"61165b7d356eb8e235b90843b9eab1b3a34f0a4991950e8103408418d8df13c6","packTokens":25301,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":1,"sections":[{"id":"side","tokens":100,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":236,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"drafts","tokens":24943,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":5,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"merge"},"pointers":[],"system":"PRODUCT SIDE. This run builds the API side of the product these requirements describe, in an existing .NET API project: every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there, and the data behind them. The web app is built in its own repo: no screen is built here, and no criterion is written for one.\n\nMerge three independent spec drafts into one spec (same format rules as the drafts).\nEvery merged requirement lists in \"alignment\" which draft requirements it came from, as \"d<draft>:<REQ-id>\" (e.g. \"d1:REQ-2\"). Keep a requirement even if only one draft has it. Never write a requirement that is in no draft.\nWhen drafts conflict, keep both readings as separate requirements and add a conflict entry. Renumber merged requirements REQ-1.. and their ACs AC-<req>.<n>.\nEach Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes. Reword a draft's Then that doesn't, without changing what it checks.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"drafts\" kind=\"spec-drafts\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d1\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"Customer authentication uses email and password followed by an email-delivered one-time code, and password reset uses an email link (ASM-1, ASM-9).\",\n   \"Operational alert delivery uses email and fixed templates; SMS and push are excluded (ASM-3, ASM-10).\",\n   \"Warehouse date calculations use its configured local time zone and configured working-day and holiday calendar (ASM-11).\",\n   \"Expiry processing runs as an application-side scheduled check and records dispatcher alerts (ASM-5).\",\n   \"The root health response, OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI remain available (ASM-7).\",\n   \"No legacy data is imported; configured setup seed data may be present as assumed in ASM-2, but business records are entered through contracted operations.\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"No later than 120 seconds after reading receipt.\",\n    \"text\": \"Excursion alerts are delivered to the driver when applicable, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers after the triggering reading is received.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n    \"metric\": \"5,000 devices reporting at once.\",\n    \"text\": \"The temperature-data processing capability supports logger and cold-room readings from devices reporting concurrently.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"Portal, customer-portal, and mobile-application screens; this run implements the API side only.\",\n   \"Uncontracted API operations and broader product workflows (Q-1).\",\n   \"Legacy spreadsheet or paper-process data migration (Q-7).\",\n   \"SMS and push notification delivery (ASM-3, ASM-10).\",\n   \"A vendor-specific logger client; readings and file processing use contracted operations and deployment-provided gateway configuration (ASM-8).\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Each operation in the locked OpenAPI document has a valid authorized request and a fixture for its required records\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status, media type, and body shape match the operation's contract-defined success response\",\n      \"when\": \"A client calls each declared operation at its declared path and method\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An operation has a contract-defined validation, authentication, authorization, missing-record, state-conflict, or server-error response\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status and error body match the corresponding contract-defined response\",\n      \"when\": \"The corresponding condition is exercised through that operation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall expose and implement every path, HTTP method, parameter, request and response schema, media type, and response status defined in the locked `contracts/openapi.yaml`, without adding contract operations.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"Q-1\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API is running\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"Each response status is 200 and the root response value is `API is up`\",\n      \"when\": \"A client requests `/`, `/openapi/v1.json`, and `/swagger`\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"anchors\": [\n     {\n      \"lineEnd\": 31,\n      \"lineStart\": 27,\n      \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n      \"quote\": \"app.UseCors();\\napp.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall continue serving the existing root health response, OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI while the contracted operations are added.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"ASM-7\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An active customer account has valid credentials and an email delivery service is configured\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains a challenge identifier and an email message contains the one-time code, with no authenticated customer result issued before code verification\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer submits credentials to the contracted sign-in operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer challenge is pending\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"Each response status and returned authentication or challenge value reflects the contract-defined outcome, and only a valid unused code produces an authenticated customer result\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer verifies a valid code, submits an invalid or reused code, or requests a resend\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer account requests a password reset\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response values identify token usability and the reset link is sent by email, and a consumed or invalid token cannot reset the password again\",\n      \"when\": \"The account requests, inspects, and completes a reset using the issued token\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The staff identity-provider authorization URL is configured\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned value is the configured URL\",\n      \"when\": \"An unauthenticated client calls the staff authorization-URL operation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement the contracted staff authorization-URL, customer email-and-password challenge, one-time-code verification and resend, and password-reset request, token-inspection, and completion flows, sending customer codes and reset links by email.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"ASM-1\",\n     \"ASM-9\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Two customer organisations have separate orders, deliveries, certificates, and recall records\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 403 or the contract-defined not-found status and contains no other-organisation record\",\n      \"when\": \"An authenticated user from one organisation lists or requests another organisation's records\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A staff member is assigned to one warehouse and a second warehouse has records\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response list contains only assigned-warehouse records and the response for an inaccessible record contains no record value\",\n      \"when\": \"The staff member lists or requests warehouse-scoped stock, receipts, routes, or quality records\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An Auditor is authenticated and a record is available\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The read response contains the record and each prohibited write response status is 403\",\n      \"when\": \"The Auditor reads the record and attempts a contracted create, update, or delete operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An account has been deactivated or removed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 and contains no protected record\",\n      \"when\": \"That account makes a subsequent authenticated API request\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall enforce the contracted role, warehouse, and customer-organisation access restrictions on every operation, including read-only Auditor access and immediate denial of access to deactivated accounts.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A permitted Warehouse Operator submits a valid receipt with product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and location\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains those submitted values and a Quarantined status\",\n      \"when\": \"The operator creates the receipt and retrieves it\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A product and lot number already have a receipt\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains a distinct receipt identifier, and the stock list reports both receipt quantities without merging their receipt records\",\n      \"when\": \"A second permitted receipt with the same product and lot number is submitted\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A receipt has an expiry date before the current date, or a Quality Officer attempts release when the expiry date is within 30 days of receipt\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 409 as defined by the operation and the receipt or release status value is not changed to Released\",\n      \"when\": \"The receipt or release action is submitted\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A valid supplier-format logger file or separate evidence file is available for an existing receipt\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains the receipt record or action result and a subsequent receipt response contains the stored file-related record or processed readings\",\n      \"when\": \"The file is uploaded through its contracted receipt operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A handling unit has a positive available quantity at a warehouse location\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains the resulting quantity and location, and a movement record contains actor, time, source, destination, and moved quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"A permitted move or opening-stock operation is submitted\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist contracted receipt, receipt-logger, receipt-evidence, stock, movement, and opening-stock records and enforce separate receipt traceability, quarantine, receipt-expiry validation, and Quality Officer release.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-3\",\n     \"Q-7\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator creates or searches for a product\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains the submitted product specification and active state, and searches return matching product records\",\n      \"when\": \"The product is submitted, listed, retrieved, or deactivated through the contracted operations\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A product has no temperature profile, or a profile submission has overlapping or discontinuous tier boundaries\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 400 and the response error identifies the invalid profile or tier values\",\n      \"when\": \"The product or profile is submitted\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A valid profile change includes an effective date, label, limits, tiers, and reason\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record and profile list contain the new version, its reason, effective date, and actor, while the previous version remains returned unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"A System Administrator creates the profile version\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A product has an earlier profile version\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 409 and the earlier profile record remains unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"A caller attempts to alter that earlier version rather than create a new version\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist searchable products and immutable versioned temperature profiles, requiring a profile for each product and validating profile tiers, effective dates, reasons, and governance history.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An authenticated customer submits an order with at least one line, positive pack quantities, an organisation-owned address, and an idempotency key\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"Both response bodies return the same order identifier and the order list contains one order\",\n      \"when\": \"The order is submitted twice with the same key and payload\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer submits a date before the serving warehouse's next eligible date or a product inactive for ordering\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 409 and no order row is created\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer places the order\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Released stock is available for an order from its serving warehouse\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record shows earliest-expiry eligible lots first, applies minimum remaining shelf life, uses the greater stability-budget usage first for tied expiry dates, and exposes each allocation and outstanding quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"The order is allocated\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Suitable stock is insufficient for a partial order or any line of a complete-only order\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The partial order response shows allocated and outstanding quantities without over-allocating stock, while the complete-only order holds no stock until every line can be fully allocated\",\n      \"when\": \"Allocation is attempted\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Multiple orders are submitted concurrently against the same available handling units\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response records and stock list show no unit allocated to more than one order and total allocated quantity does not exceed physical available quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"The allocations are committed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits an allocation override with a reason, or without a reason, or to stock that violates Released status or customer shelf life\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.6\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The valid response record includes the reason and changed allocation, while each invalid response status is 400 or 409 and the original allocation remains unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"The override operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Suitable stock is released for waiting back orders or allocated stock becomes On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, or Expired\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.7\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The order response records show oldest-first back-order allocation or removed allocations and replacements, and an alert email call records the resulting dispatcher notification\",\n      \"when\": \"The allocation service updates affected orders\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer order is not yet Packed, or has already reached Packed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.8\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status and order status value reflect the applicable lifecycle rule, and successful cancellation returns the allocated quantity to available stock\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer attempts to change or cancel it, or a permitted dispatcher cancels it\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist customer orders and dispatch allocations using the serving warehouse's configured cut-off, working-day, holiday, time-zone, and customer shelf-life rules, and enforce idempotency, pre-packing customer changes, and the specified suitable-stock allocation and back-order rules.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-4\",\n     \"ASM-6\",\n     \"ASM-11\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator submits a pack request for available allocated stock\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains the box, logger, lot quantities, operator, and seal time; a reused logger or incompatible packing response status is 409\",\n      \"when\": \"The requested box contains one logger, products with the same storage band, and a compatible box type\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits a route with a date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains the requested route values, and confirmation is refused with a 409 response containing the box and qualification shortfall when a box exceeds qualified duration less the configured safety margin\",\n      \"when\": \"The route is created, updated, or confirmed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver calls route listing, route detail, scan, or departure operations for the authenticated driver\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response list or record contains only that driver's authorized route, ordered stops, expected boxes, scans, and departure state\",\n      \"when\": \"The driver supplies the contracted date or route data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver synchronizes queued actions with distinct action identifiers or submits the same action identifier more than once\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains accepted and conflicting actions, and the resulting route history contains each accepted action only once\",\n      \"when\": \"The synchronization operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver submits a handover with receiver, acknowledgement, signature, photo, completion time, location availability, and box delivery or refusal quantities\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record and subsequent delivery-evidence response contain the persisted evidence and quantities, and refused quantities retain the refusal reason\",\n      \"when\": \"The handover operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A confirmed route is changed before its driver has left for the affected stop\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.6\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains the changed schedule or stop order and an email call records notification to the driver\",\n      \"when\": \"A dispatcher updates the route\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist compatible box packing and route plans, enforce box and route qualification, and record driver loading, departure, synchronization, handover, refusal, and delivery-evidence operations.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-1\",\n     \"ASM-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A contracted receipt logger upload contains repeated, late, out-of-order, future-dated, or pre-sealing readings\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record places readings at their occurred times, stores a duplicate once, flags future and pre-sealing readings as excluded from calculations, and shows unavailable-reading gaps\",\n      \"when\": \"The file is processed and temperature history is requested for its entity and date range\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Three consecutive in-band readings follow an out-of-band reading in a persisted history\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response records show the excursion open from the first out-of-band reading until the third consecutive in-band reading and show time charged to each applicable tier\",\n      \"when\": \"The related temperature history and handling-unit record are requested\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A handling unit has excursion history, or a late reading changes that history\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record shows separate budgets for portions with different histories, updated remaining tier allowances, excursion links, holds, and an audit event for the correction\",\n      \"when\": \"The handling-unit or temperature-history operation is called after recalculation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An excursion begins, a tier allowance falls below 25 percent, a tier is exhausted, or a not-permitted range is reached\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"An email call is recorded for the required driver when on-route, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers, and affected stock response records have On Hold status pending a decision\",\n      \"when\": \"The triggering reading is received and processed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A logger has sent no reading for 15 minutes and its box is out for delivery\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record marks the device silent, shows the gap, and an alert email call is recorded\",\n      \"when\": \"The silent-device check is run and temperature history is requested\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A cold room or its temperature records are available\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.6\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response list or record contains the latest reading, status, gaps, alerts, history timestamps, and applicable band and excursion markers\",\n      \"when\": \"A caller lists cold rooms, retrieves one cold room, or requests temperature history for the room, box, lot, handling unit, or device\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall expose temperature histories for contracted entity types and persist available logger readings, gaps, excursions, tier-by-tier handling-unit budgets, related holds, and corrected history when readings arrive late or out of order.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-3\",\n     \"ASM-4\",\n     \"ASM-8\",\n     \"ASM-10\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Officer submits a disposition proposal with disposition, reason, and identity confirmation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains the proposal and actor, the same officer cannot approve it, and a decision by a different eligible manager records the approval or return without replacing the proposal\",\n      \"when\": \"The proposal is retrieved or a decision is submitted by the proposing officer or an eligible different Quality Manager\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A quality decision exists and an authorized caller submits a separately signed superseding decision\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains the new decision and the earlier decision remains available in the returned decision history\",\n      \"when\": \"The supersede operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Rejected stock has a positive quantity to destroy\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains those values and the destroyed quantity is removed from available stock\",\n      \"when\": \"An authorized caller submits a destruction date, quantity, and witness\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An eligible Quality Manager starts a signed recall for selected product lots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response records identify affected stock, warehouse locations, boxes, routes, deliveries, and customer response progress, and recalled held stock is unavailable for allocation\",\n      \"when\": \"The recall is started and its record and trace are requested\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer submits or updates a recall response for an authorized delivery\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains on-hand, used, destroyed, and stated-disposition values and the recall progress reflects the submitted quantities\",\n      \"when\": \"The recall response operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A recall has unaccounted quantity or all quantity is accounted for\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.6\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 409 for closure with unaccounted quantity and no valid write-off, or the response record contains the signed closure or write-off when its preconditions are met\",\n      \"when\": \"A Quality Manager submits closure or a signed write-off\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist quality cases, signed proposals and decisions, superseding decisions, destruction records, and recalls, applying the required two-person quality approval and recall-accounting rules.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-3\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"Q-6\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An authenticated customer requests orders, deliveries, delivery details, certificates, certificate files, or recall notices\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response list, record, or PDF file contains only records belonging to that customer's organisation\",\n      \"when\": \"The corresponding customer operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator submits a valid saved address or invitation, changes an address, or removes an address or team member within their organisation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record or action result identifies the change and subsequent lists contain the updated organisation-scoped address or team record\",\n      \"when\": \"The contracted customer-administration operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator attempts to edit or remove an address or member belonging to another organisation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 403 or the contract-defined not-found status and no other-organisation row is changed\",\n      \"when\": \"The contracted customer-administration operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An authenticated customer account has a saved language preference\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record contains the saved language value, and a value outside the contract enum returns status 400\",\n      \"when\": \"The account is retrieved and patched with `en` or `ar`\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement customer organisation account, address, team, delivery, certificate, recall-notice, order, and language-preference operations with all returned records and mutations scoped to the authenticated organisation.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"ASM-1\",\n     \"ASM-9\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator requests organizations, organization details, accounts, or account details\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response list or record contains the persisted organization, member, address, shelf-life, role, and access-assignment values within the caller's authorization scope\",\n      \"when\": \"The corresponding list or retrieval operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator creates, updates, deactivates an account, or updates an organization's minimum remaining shelf life\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status and record or action result reflect the new account state, roles, assignments, or minimum shelf-life value\",\n      \"when\": \"The contracted administration operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An authorized caller requests an operational report for a permitted date range and warehouse or requests a lot history\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response record or list contains only authorized report values and chronologically ordered receipt, movement, delivery, and destruction events for the requested lot\",\n      \"when\": \"The report or lot-history operation is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement contracted administration, operational-report, and lot-history operations, persisting organization shelf-life settings, account role and warehouse assignments, and chronological business records.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A consequential contracted change or decision is successfully recorded\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response list contains the event's actor, timestamp, action type, and affected record and applies the supplied filters\",\n      \"when\": \"An authorized caller queries audit events using supported search, date, action-type, or user filters\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An audit event has been recorded\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response list still contains the event and a write attempt against the audit event returns status 403\",\n      \"when\": \"Time passes and the event is queried again\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall store the actor and timestamp for each consequential contracted change and decision in read-only audit events and retain those events without automatic expiry.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"Q-6\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The database configuration is invalid\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.1\",\n      \"level\": \"manual\",\n      \"then\": \"The process exits before serving contracted operations and the startup output contains an error\",\n      \"when\": \"The API process starts\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API is running and its configured database becomes unavailable during a contracted operation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 500 with the contract-defined `server_error` code and no success response or success record is returned\",\n      \"when\": \"The operation is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If persistent storage configuration is invalid, then the Meridian API shall fail startup, and if a contracted operation fails because persistent storage is unavailable, then the API shall return the contract-defined server-error response without reporting the business operation as successful.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-8\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A new configured database contains no API-entered business records and legacy spreadsheet or paper data exists outside the API\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The database contains no imported legacy business row\",\n      \"when\": \"The API starts\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall start without importing legacy spreadsheet or paper-process business records and shall persist business data through contracted operations only.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-7\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A handling unit is allocated and reaches the end of its expiry date\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.1\",\n      \"level\": \"job\",\n      \"then\": \"The database row has Expired status, the order response no longer lists that allocation, an audit event records the change, and an alert email call is recorded for the dispatcher\",\n      \"when\": \"The scheduled expiry check runs\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a handling unit reaches the end of its expiry date, the Meridian API shall automatically mark it Expired, remove it from allocations, record the change, and alert the dispatcher.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-3\",\n     \"ASM-5\",\n     \"ASM-10\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"suggestions\": [\n   \"Add a locked-contract operation for authenticated batch ingestion of live logger and cold-room readings, with an explicit gateway authentication and duplicate-reading contract; the current contract exposes temperature-history retrieval and receipt logger-file upload but no general telemetry-ingestion operation.\",\n   \"If product codes and warehouse cut-off, time-zone, holiday, and working-day settings are required to be managed through the API, add their fields and contracted configuration operations before requiring clients to maintain them.\",\n   \"Specify the exact customer password-reset token expiry and one-time-code expiry/attempt limits in the contract or authentication policy.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d2\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"Customer authentication uses email and password with one-time-code verification; password-reset links are sent by email, with no social or single sign-on integration (ASM-1, ASM-9).\",\n   \"Staff identity-provider authorization URL and database, email-sender, warehouse cutoff, safety-margin, local-time-zone, and calendar values are supplied by deployment or warehouse configuration; no additional configuration API is added (ASM-1, ASM-3, ASM-6, ASM-11).\",\n   \"A scheduled application-side expiry check performs the stock expiry transition and records a dispatcher alert (ASM-5).\",\n   \"The existing root health response, generated OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI remain available (ASM-7).\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"100% of audit rows created by consequential-operation tests have non-empty actor and event-time fields; 0 audit rows are automatically expired.\",\n    \"text\": \"Consequential-operation audit events contain an actor and event time and are retained without automatic expiry.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"Portal screens, customer web pages, staff web pages, and iOS/Android mobile-client implementation or local offline storage.\",\n   \"Legacy spreadsheet and paper-record migration (Q-7).\",\n   \"Business API operations and workflows not exposed in contracts/openapi.yaml (Q-1).\",\n   \"A vendor-specific logger-gateway client or an additional inbound-temperature API not present in the locked contract (Q-1, ASM-8).\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A table of every method and path in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, with a valid fixture for each operation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status, response media type, and response body fields match that operation's declared successful response\",\n      \"when\": \"Each operation is called using its declared method, path, parameters, headers, and request media type\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A table of each operation's declared invalid-input, authorization, not-found, conflict, and server-error cases\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status and response body fields match a response declared for that operation in the contract\",\n      \"when\": \"Each applicable case is sent to the documented operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API is running\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 200 for each call, and the OpenAPI response includes the contracted `/api` operations\",\n      \"when\": \"A client calls `/`, `/openapi/v1.json`, and `/swagger`\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"anchors\": [\n     {\n      \"lineEnd\": 31,\n      \"lineStart\": 28,\n      \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n      \"quote\": \"app.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement every method, path, parameter, header, media type, request and response schema, and status code defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml` under `/api`, expose no uncontracted business operation, and preserve the existing root health response, OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"Q-1\",\n     \"ASM-7\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A valid contracted create or update request for a persisted resource\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is successful and the returned record fields match the persisted row\",\n      \"when\": \"The request succeeds and the resource is fetched through its contracted read operation after an API process restart\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A contracted upload operation receives a valid evidence or logger file\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is successful and the returned file or record fields match the uploaded content and metadata\",\n      \"when\": \"The related contracted read or download operation is called after an API process restart\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"anchors\": [\n     {\n      \"lineEnd\": 7,\n      \"lineStart\": 5,\n      \"path\": \"App.Api/AppDb.cs\",\n      \"quote\": \"public class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\\n{\\n}\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist and serve the records, relationships, state changes, and file artifacts needed by every contracted operation from a shared database, with successful mutations remaining available after process restart.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-1\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The staff identity-provider authorization URL is configured\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response body contains the configured authorization URL\",\n      \"when\": \"An unauthenticated client calls `GET /api/auth/staff/authorization-url`\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer account has valid credentials and an eligible one-time-code challenge\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status and response body contain the challenge and authentication result fields defined by the contract\",\n      \"when\": \"The client calls customer sign-in, code resend, and code verification with the contract request fields\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer requests a password reset and then submits a valid reset token and new password\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status and response body report the contract-defined action result, and the configured email sender receives the reset-link request\",\n      \"when\": \"The client calls the password-reset request, token-inspection, and completion operations\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall provide staff authorization-URL lookup and customer email-and-password sign-in, one-time-code verification and resend, and email password-reset request, token inspection, and completion through their matching contract operations.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"ASM-1\",\n     \"ASM-9\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer account belongs to organisation A and an order or delivery belongs to organisation B\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is forbidden or not found as declared by the operation, and the response contains no record fields belonging to organisation B\",\n      \"when\": \"The account calls the corresponding customer list or detail operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A staff account is assigned to warehouse A but not warehouse B\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 403 and the response contains no record fields from warehouse B\",\n      \"when\": \"The account lists or fetches warehouse-scoped stock, receipts, orders, or routes in warehouse B\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An Auditor account has read access and a separate write-capable role is not assigned\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The read response status is successful and the write response status is 403\",\n      \"when\": \"The Auditor calls an allowed read operation and then a contracted create, update, or delete operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An account has been deactivated\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 and no protected record is returned\",\n      \"when\": \"That account presents its existing credentials or token to a protected contracted operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Manager or Auditor is authenticated\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is successful and the returned record belongs to the requested warehouse\",\n      \"when\": \"That account reads a record from a warehouse outside an ordinary staff member's assignment\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When an authenticated caller invokes a contracted operation, the Meridian API shall enforce the caller's staff role, assigned warehouse scope, customer-organisation scope, and Auditor read-only restriction, and reject disabled accounts.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A product create or update request omits a valid profile, or a proposed profile contains overlapping tiers or a gap\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 400 and the response body contains the contract-defined error fields\",\n      \"when\": \"The product or profile operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A valid temperature profile includes its reason, effective date, limits, and tiers\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains a new version with the actor and effective-date fields, and the earlier version's returned value is unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"An authorized administrator creates the profile and later lists profile versions\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A product is deactivated\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 409 as declared by the operation and the response does not report a successful order\",\n      \"when\": \"A customer submits an order line for that product\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where product administration is used, the Meridian API shall require a temperature profile for each product and create immutable historical profile versions with a reason, effective date, and actor while validating tier boundaries for overlap and gaps.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-1\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Two receipt requests have the same product and lot number but separate receipt submissions\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response and persisted rows contain two separately identifiable receipt records for that product and lot\",\n      \"when\": \"Both valid requests are submitted and the receipt collection is fetched\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A valid receipt request is submitted\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains a Quarantined status and the recorded product, lot, expiry-date, quantity, supplier, and location fields\",\n      \"when\": \"The receipt is fetched before any Quality Officer release decision\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A receipt expiry date is in the past, or the stock is within 30 days of expiry on arrival\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status rejects the past-expiry receipt or the release, and the response contains an error or conflict value\",\n      \"when\": \"The receipt is submitted or a release decision is attempted, respectively\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A receipt has an uploaded supplier-format logger file and the caller is a Quality Officer\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains the inbound readings and the budget-used value needed for the release decision\",\n      \"when\": \"The logger upload is processed and the receipt is fetched before release\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where a receipt is created, uploaded, released, or queried, the Meridian API shall retain a separate traceable receipt for each submission, quarantine received stock until Quality Officer release, and reject past-expiry receipts or release of stock within 30 days of expiry on arrival.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A released handling unit has passed its expiry date and is allocated to an order\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.1\",\n      \"level\": \"job\",\n      \"then\": \"The stock row status is Expired, the allocation count for that unit is zero, and an alert row identifies the dispatcher notification\",\n      \"when\": \"The scheduled expiry check runs\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a handling unit passes its expiry date, the Meridian API's scheduled expiry check shall mark it Expired, remove its allocations, and record a dispatcher alert.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"ASM-5\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An order request has at least one line, a quantity of at least one pack per line, an organisation-owned address, and a valid delivery date\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"Both responses identify one order and the persisted order count for that key is one\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer submits the request with an idempotency key and repeats the same request using that key\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A submitted order has an invalid line, an address belonging to another organisation, or a requested date earlier than the serving warehouse's cut-off, working-day, and holiday rules permit\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 409 as declared by the operation and the response does not contain a successful order record\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer submits the order\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An order is not yet Packed, or has already reached Packed status\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is successful for the pre-packing change or cancellation and is 409 for the post-packing request\",\n      \"when\": \"The authenticated customer attempts to change or cancel the order\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer cancels an order with allocated stock before packing\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response reports Cancelled and the available-stock value increases by the released allocation quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"The cancellation operation completes and stock is listed\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a customer submits, changes, or cancels an order, the Meridian API shall validate its lines, saved organisation address, requested delivery date and fulfillment preference, accept a repeated submission only once per idempotency key, and permit customer changes or cancellation only before packing.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-4\",\n     \"ASM-6\",\n     \"ASM-11\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A line has multiple eligible released lots with different expiry dates and one customer minimum shelf-life rule\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned allocation list uses the earliest-expiring suitable lot first and contains no lot below the minimum remaining shelf life\",\n      \"when\": \"The order is allocated\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Two eligible lots have the same expiry date but different stability-budget usage\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The returned allocation list uses the lot with more budget used first\",\n      \"when\": \"The order is allocated\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Several orders concurrently request the same limited stock quantity\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The sum of returned allocated quantities does not exceed the stock row's physical available quantity and no stock row is allocated to two orders\",\n      \"when\": \"The order submissions are processed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A complete-only order cannot be fully allocated, or a partial order can be partly allocated\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The complete-only order holds zero allocated stock until it can be filled, while the partial order shows its outstanding quantity and older eligible back orders receive released stock first\",\n      \"when\": \"The order is submitted and suitable stock is later released\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits an allocation override with a reason for an eligible alternative lot, or for a lot that violates release or shelf-life rules\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The eligible override response contains the new allocation and reason, while the invalid override response status is 400 or 409 and the allocation row remains unchanged\",\n      \"when\": \"The override operation is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When stock is allocated to an order, the Meridian API shall allocate only released, physically available stock that meets the customer's minimum remaining shelf life, select earliest expiry first with the stated budget-used tie-break, and apply the complete-order, partial-order, back-order, and override rules.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A pack request has a compatible product band, box type, and one logger, or has incompatible bands or a logger already assigned to another open box\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The compatible response records the contents and logger fields, while the incompatible response status is 400 or 409 and no conflicting pack row is created\",\n      \"when\": \"The pack operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A route has a vehicle, driver, date, and at least one ordered stop with planned arrival times\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains the persisted route and stop sequence, and a conflicting driver or vehicle assignment returns status 409\",\n      \"when\": \"The route is created, changed, and confirmed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A route's packed box would exceed its qualified duration less the configured safety margin at a planned arrival\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 409 and the response message identifies the box and the amount by which the margin is exceeded\",\n      \"when\": \"The route confirmation operation is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A confirmed route has a stop not yet departed for\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains the updated route record and a driver-change event is recorded\",\n      \"when\": \"A dispatcher changes its stop order or schedule\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When stock is packed or a dispatch route is created, changed, or confirmed, the Meridian API shall enforce box and product temperature compatibility, logger association, route resource availability, stop order and planned times, and the qualified-duration safety margin.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"ASM-6\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver is assigned to today's route and another route belongs to a different driver\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response includes the assigned route and returns status 403 or 404 for the other driver's route\",\n      \"when\": \"The driver lists and fetches routes and submits a scan or departure for each\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver submits queued loading, handover, or refusal actions with action identifiers and occurrence times\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains a result for each submitted action and persisted event rows retain each action identifier and occurrence time\",\n      \"when\": \"The driver synchronization operation completes\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver submits a valid handover with a receiver, signature, photo, completion time, and delivered or refused box quantities\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response and evidence record contain the submitted signature, photo, quantities, acknowledgement, and refusal fields\",\n      \"when\": \"The handover operation completes and authorized evidence is fetched\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When an authenticated driver reads a route, records a scan or departure, synchronizes queued actions, or submits a handover, the Meridian API shall scope route access to that driver and persist the submitted action time, delivery quantities, signature, photo, acknowledgements, and refusal evidence.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A handling unit has recorded temperature history with an interval containing no readings and a stored profile band\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains readings in recorded-time order, an explicit gap, and the temperature-band and excursion fields for the requested interval\",\n      \"when\": \"The caller fetches temperature history for the unit or its box, lot, device, or cold room\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A handling unit has tiered budget usage and a related quality case\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains the used and remaining value for each tier and the linked case telemetry and decision fields\",\n      \"when\": \"An authorized Quality Officer fetches the unit and quality case\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Officer proposes a disposition and a Quality Manager submits an approval or return decision\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response and persisted decision rows identify the disposition, reason, decision status, and decision actor\",\n      \"when\": \"The disposition and proposal-decision operations are called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a caller requests a contracted temperature history, stock handling unit, cold-room, or quality case, the Meridian API shall return the persisted readings, gaps, temperature bands, excursions, tier budget values, related stock, and recorded quality decisions applicable to that resource.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-1\",\n     \"Q-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Manager starts a recall for a product and selected lots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains the recalled lot identifiers, held-stock rows, and linked warehouse, box, route, and delivery records\",\n      \"when\": \"The recall and trace operations are called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer organisation has a delivery associated with a recalled lot\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains only that organisation's notice and records the on-hand, used, destroyed, and stated-disposition values\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer lists recall notices and submits or updates its delivery response\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A recall has outstanding quantity that is not accounted for\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The first response status is 409 and the later response reports the write-off record and updated accounted quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"A Quality Manager attempts to close it without a signed write-off, then submits a signed write-off for the remaining quantity\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a Quality Manager starts, traces, receives customer responses for, closes, or writes off a recall, the Meridian API shall retain the signed recall actions, block affected stock still held, and expose the lot-to-customer trace and outstanding quantities until they are accounted for or signed off.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-1\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer administrator is authenticated for organisation A\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains only organisation A's records and a request targeting another organisation returns status 403 or 404\",\n      \"when\": \"The administrator lists, invites, updates, or removes team members and lists, saves, updates, or removes addresses\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An account preference uses a language value declared by the contract\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response contains the saved `en` or `ar` language value\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer account preference is updated and then fetched\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An authorized caller requests an operational report, delivery certificate, delivery evidence, or lot history\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is successful and its returned record, file, or list fields match the persisted source records and requested filters\",\n      \"when\": \"The matching contracted read or download operation is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where contracted organisation, account, address, team, preference, report, certificate, evidence, or lot-history operations are used, the Meridian API shall read and persist their contract-defined records within the authenticated caller's permitted organisation and role scope.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-1\",\n     \"Q-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An authenticated actor performs a consequential contracted mutation or decision\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response list and audit row contain the actor, event time, and action type\",\n      \"when\": \"The operation completes and the authorized audit-events operation is queried for the actor and time range\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An audit event has been persisted\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The event row remains available and the response list still contains the event\",\n      \"when\": \"The database date is advanced beyond the event date and audit events are queried\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a consequential contracted operation changes data or records a decision, the Meridian API shall persist an audit event with the acting account and event time and retain that event without automatic expiry.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"Q-6\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API is started with an invalid database connection configuration\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The process reports startup failure and does not serve a successful business-operation response\",\n      \"when\": \"Application startup initializes the configured database\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API is running and the database becomes unavailable during a contracted mutation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The response status is 500, the response body contains the contract-defined problem code and message fields, and no successful record is returned\",\n      \"when\": \"The operation is called\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"anchors\": [\n     {\n      \"lineEnd\": 9,\n      \"lineStart\": 8,\n      \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n      \"quote\": \"builder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDb>(o => o.UseNpgsql(builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\\\"App\\\")\\n    ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\\\"No database connection is configured. Set ConnectionStrings__App (for example Host=...;Port=5432;Database=...;Username=...;Password=«SECRET_1»\")));\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"lineEnd\": 22,\n      \"lineStart\": 20,\n      \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n      \"quote\": \"        using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"If the database configuration is invalid at startup or the database fails during a contracted operation, then the Meridian API shall fail startup or return that operation's contract-defined 500 server-error response without reporting success.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n    \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-8\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A deployment environment contains legacy spreadsheet or paper-process records but no records entered through the contracted API\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-17.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"The database row count for imported legacy business records is zero and the response lists contain no imported legacy records\",\n      \"when\": \"The API starts and its contracted collection operations are queried\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall not import legacy spreadsheet or paper-process business records and shall create operational records through the contracted API operations.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-7\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"suggestions\": [\n   \"Provide deployment and warehouse configuration values for the identity provider, email sender, cutoffs, safety margins, time zones, and working-day calendars before acceptance testing.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d3\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"Customer one-time codes and password-reset links are delivered by email as assumed in ASM-1 and ASM-9.\",\n   \"Staff authorization uses the configured identity-provider URL; customer authentication uses email, password, and one-time-code verification.\",\n   \"The configured PostgreSQL database is the source of persistence, and legacy spreadsheet or paper data is not imported.\",\n   \"The scheduled expiry check executes at the end of the stock expiry date, uses controlled time in testing, and stores a dispatcher alert record.\",\n   \"Warehouse cut-off, working-day, holiday, time-zone, safety-margin, and email settings are supplied by existing deployment configuration or contracted data rather than new API operations.\",\n   \"The temperature-history and excursion behaviors operate on data available through contracted receipt logger uploads and persisted contracted records; no uncontracted logger-ingestion endpoint is introduced.\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"Each alert email is sent no later than 120 seconds after the triggering reading is received.\",\n    \"text\": \"For a temperature excursion detected while processing a contracted logger file, the API sends alerts to the affected driver when applicable, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers through the configured email channel within the stated two-minute window.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"API operations and business workflows not exposed by contracts/openapi.yaml (Q-1).\",\n   \"Migration of legacy spreadsheet and paper-process business data (Q-7).\",\n   \"Web portal and mobile application screens; this run implements the product-side API only.\",\n   \"Social sign-in, single sign-on alternatives, SMS, push notifications, and vendor-specific logger clients (ASM-1, ASM-3, ASM-8, ASM-9, ASM-10).\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"the operation matrix in contracts/openapi.yaml and valid authorized fixtures for each operation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"each response status and response body conform to that operation's declared responses and schemas\",\n      \"when\": \"a test sends a request to every declared method and path\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a request with an invalid body, missing authentication, inaccessible record, or conflicting state for an operation declaring that error\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status and error body match one of the operation's declared error responses\",\n      \"when\": \"the request is sent to the declared method and path\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a path and method absent from contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status is 404 or 405 and no business record is created\",\n      \"when\": \"a request is sent to that path and method\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement every HTTP method and path in contracts/openapi.yaml with its declared request schema, response schema, and status codes, without adding uncontracted API operations.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"Q-1\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a customer account with valid email and password\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response first contains a verification challenge and only the verified response contains an authenticated customer credential\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer calls signInCustomer and then verifyCustomerCode with its valid challenge code\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a customer account with an active verification challenge\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response reports the challenge or reset action and an email message is issued for the code or reset link\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer calls resendCustomerCode or requests a password reset and subsequently inspects or completes a valid reset token\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an authenticated customer, staff member, Quality Manager, or Auditor with configured organization, warehouse, and role assignments\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response contains no other customer's records or unassigned-warehouse records and unauthorized writes return the contract-defined status\",\n      \"when\": \"the principal reads or attempts to change contracted records outside its allowed scope or permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an Auditor credential and an active or deactivated account credential\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status denies the Auditor write and deactivated-account access\",\n      \"when\": \"the Auditor attempts a write or a deactivated account calls a protected operation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"the configured staff identity-provider authorization URL\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record contains that configured URL\",\n      \"when\": \"an authorized client calls getStaffAuthorizationUrl\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall authenticate customer users with email and password followed by one-time-code verification, provide the configured staff identity-provider authorization URL, and enforce account, organization, warehouse, and role access restrictions on contracted operations.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"ASM-1\",\n     \"ASM-9\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an empty configured database and valid input to a contracted create or update operation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"a database row for the submitted record remains and the corresponding contracted read returns that record\",\n      \"when\": \"the operation returns success and the application is restarted\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"legacy spreadsheet or paper-process records that are not submitted through contracted operations\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response lists contain no imported business records from those legacy sources\",\n      \"when\": \"the API starts with its configured database\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist the business records and relationships required by contracted operations in the configured database while leaving legacy spreadsheet and paper-process data unimported.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-7\",\n     \"ASM-2\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a Warehouse Operator authorized for a warehouse and valid receipt data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"each response record has a distinct receipt identity, each stored receipt has Quarantined status, and listReceipts returns the separate receipt records\",\n      \"when\": \"the operator calls createReceipt, including repeatedly for the same product and lot number\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a receipt with an expiry date before the current date or a receipt whose expiry is within 30 days of arrival\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status rejects the expired receipt or refuses release of the near-expiry stock\",\n      \"when\": \"the operator attempts receipt creation or an authorized Quality Officer attempts release, respectively\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an existing authorized receipt and a valid supplier-format logger file or separate evidence file\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record or action result identifies the accepted upload and getReceipt returns the associated file or processed inbound readings\",\n      \"when\": \"uploadReceiptLogger or uploadReceiptEvidence is called with the file\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an authorized Quality Officer decision for a quarantined receipt\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record shows the decision actor and time and the stock status is Released\",\n      \"when\": \"the contracted quality disposition workflow records a release decision\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a handling unit with a valid source and destination location and quantity\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the returned record includes the source, destination, quantity, actor, and movement time\",\n      \"when\": \"moveStock records a move and listMoves or getLotHistory is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"stock whose expiry date has ended and which is allocated to an order\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.6\",\n      \"level\": \"job\",\n      \"then\": \"the stock row has Expired status, its allocation row is removed, and a dispatcher alert row records the expiry outcome\",\n      \"when\": \"the scheduled expiry check runs\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where the contract exposes receipt and stock operations, the Meridian API shall persist each receipt separately, quarantine received stock, process submitted inbound logger and evidence files, and enforce the stated receipt, release, movement, and expiry rules.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"Q-3\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"ASM-5\",\n     \"ASM-10\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an authenticated customer with a saved delivery address and a unique Idempotency-Key\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"both response records identify one order and the database contains one order record\",\n      \"when\": \"placeCustomerOrder is called twice with the same key and order body\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a customer order with valid product lines, delivery address, delivery date, and deliver-complete or deliver-available choice\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record contains the submitted lines and the order's allocation and outstanding quantities\",\n      \"when\": \"placeCustomerOrder is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"released, unallocated stock in the serving warehouse, customer minimum shelf-life settings, and a submitted order\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record shows earliest-expiry eligible stock first, excludes stock below the minimum shelf life, never allocates more than available quantity, and splits a line across lots when required\",\n      \"when\": \"the API allocates the order\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an order marked deliver-complete only with insufficient suitable released stock, or an older back order awaiting stock\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record shows no stock held by the incomplete deliver-complete order and shows eligible back orders filled in submission order\",\n      \"when\": \"allocation is attempted or suitable stock is released\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an order before packing or an order already Packed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status permits the pre-packing change or cancellation and rejects the post-packing customer change or cancellation, and cancelled allocation rows are returned to available stock\",\n      \"when\": \"its customer calls changeCustomerOrder or cancelCustomerOrder\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a dispatcher allocation override with a reason that selects a lot\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.6\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status is 409 and no allocation row is changed\",\n      \"when\": \"overrideOrderAllocation is called with stock that is unreleased, unavailable, or below the customer's minimum shelf life\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a valid configured warehouse cut-off, working-day calendar, holiday calendar, and warehouse time zone\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.7\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record accepts no date earlier than the next working day before cut-off or the working day after that when submitted after cut-off\",\n      \"when\": \"a customer requests an order delivery date\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where the contract exposes customer-order and allocation operations, the Meridian API shall enforce customer ownership, pre-packing change and cancellation, duplicate-submission protection, and the specified stock allocation and back-order rules.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"Q-4\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"ASM-6\",\n     \"ASM-11\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"stock units, a box type, and a logger identifier\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status rejects the pack and no box-content or logger-assignment row is created\",\n      \"when\": \"packBox is called with no logger, a logger already assigned to another open box, incompatible product bands, or stock not available for packing\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a valid pack request and route with vehicle, driver, route date, ordered stops, and planned arrivals\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response records contain the box contents, logger, route stop sequence, planned arrival times, vehicle, and driver\",\n      \"when\": \"createDispatchRoute and packBox are called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a route whose box arrival would exceed its qualified duration less the configured safety margin, or a driver or vehicle already assigned to an overlapping route\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status refuses the conflicting operation and the response record identifies the affected box and duration overrun or overlapping assignment\",\n      \"when\": \"confirmDispatchRoute or createDispatchRoute is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an authenticated driver and a route assigned to that driver\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status and response record identify the assigned route and persisted scan, departure, or synchronized action\",\n      \"when\": \"the driver calls listDriverRoutes, getDriverRoute, scanRouteBox, confirmDriverDeparture, or synchronizeDriverActions with contract-valid inputs\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a handover for an assigned route stop with signature, photo, receiver, completion time, and box delivery or refusal data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record and getDeliveryEvidence response retain the submitted handover and its signature, photo, delivered quantities, and refusal evidence\",\n      \"when\": \"recordDriverHandover is called and authorized delivery evidence is subsequently requested\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a confirmed route with a stop not yet departed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.6\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record reflects the changed route and a driver notification row is recorded\",\n      \"when\": \"a dispatcher updates the route stop order or schedule\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where the contract exposes box, route, and driver operations, the Meridian API shall enforce packing and route constraints and persist driver scans, departure, synchronized actions, handovers, and delivery evidence.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"Q-5\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a box, lot, handling unit, device, or cold room with stored readings and reading gaps\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record returns readings in occurrence-time order, represents gaps as gaps, and includes the applicable temperature band, excursions, and handling-unit budget values\",\n      \"when\": \"getTemperatureHistory, getHandlingUnit, getColdRoom, or getQualityCase is called with an authorized identity\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an accepted processed reading outside a product's temperature band\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response records show an excursion opened by the outside-band reading, the tier-specific budget charged, and affected stock placed On Hold until a decision is recorded\",\n      \"when\": \"the associated history and quality case are read\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a logger reading in a submitted file that is late or out of order and changes a previously calculated excursion\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record shows the recalculated history, budget, hold, and excursion and an audit event row records the correction\",\n      \"when\": \"the logger file is processed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a Quality Officer proposal and a Quality Manager approval request for that proposal\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record stores the proposal actor and time and a different eligible Quality Manager is required to approve or return it\",\n      \"when\": \"proposeDisposition and decideQualityProposal are called, including an approval by the proposing person\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a decision already recorded for a quality case or rejected stock\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record contains the separately signed superseding decision or destruction details and actor and time\",\n      \"when\": \"supersedeDecision or recordDestruction is called with valid identity confirmation and required reason, date, quantity, or witness\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where the contract exposes temperature-history and quality operations, the Meridian API shall return chronological readings and gaps, maintain excursion and handling-unit budget records from processed readings, and enforce the contracted quality-decision workflow.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"Q-6\",\n     \"ASM-3\",\n     \"ASM-4\",\n     \"ASM-8\",\n     \"ASM-10\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a Quality Manager authorized to start a recall and one or more selected lots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record contains the signed recall, affected stock status, trace summary, and outstanding customer response quantities\",\n      \"when\": \"startRecall is called and the recall is subsequently read\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a started recall with affected warehouse, box, route, and delivery records\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response lists contain the chronological trace of the lot through the warehouse, boxes, routes, deliveries, movements, and destruction records\",\n      \"when\": \"getRecallTrace and getLotHistory are called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an authenticated customer organization with a delivery affected by a recall\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response lists contain only that organization's recall notices and the response record contains its reported quantities and disposition\",\n      \"when\": \"listCustomerRecallNotices and submitRecallResponse are called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a recall with outstanding unaccounted quantity\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response status rejects closure and no closed recall record is stored\",\n      \"when\": \"closeRecall is called without accounting for that quantity or a valid Quality Manager write-off\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a recall whose affected quantity is accounted for or has an authorized signed write-off\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record contains the closure or write-off decision, actor, and time\",\n      \"when\": \"closeRecall or writeOffRecallRemainder is called with valid signed input\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where the contract exposes recall operations, the Meridian API shall trace selected lots through stock and delivery records, block affected stock still held, and persist customer responses and signed recall closure decisions.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"Q-6\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a Customer Administrator authenticated for an organization\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.1\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response records and lists contain only that organization's addresses and members and reject an attempt to alter another organization's record\",\n      \"when\": \"the administrator lists, creates, edits, or removes that organization's addresses or lists, invites, or removes a team member\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an authenticated customer account with a supported language preference\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.2\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record returns or persists that account's language preference and organization settings\",\n      \"when\": \"getCustomerAccount or updateCustomerAccount is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"a System Administrator submitting product and temperature profile data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.3\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response record shows the product specification, active state, or new profile version, including its effective date, reason, and actor\",\n      \"when\": \"createProduct, updateProduct, deactivateProduct, or createTemperatureProfile is called\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an existing versioned product temperature profile\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.4\",\n      \"level\": \"api\",\n      \"then\": \"the response list retains earlier profile versions unchanged and rejects a profile with overlapping or invalid temperature tiers\",\n      \"when\": \"a new profile version is created or the profile list is read\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"an administrator updating an organization shelf-life rule or an account's roles and warehouse assignments\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.5\",\n      \"level\": \"api\